From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:41:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Conceal lost MLow packets with the voice, not silence

A lost or undecodable MLow packet used to fade the last sample to zero in
5 ms and leave up to 60 ms of silence in the middle of a word. The decoder
now conceals it the way G.711 Appendix I does: the last pitch period,
found by normalised autocorrelation, is repeated (widened to two and then
three periods so a longer loss does not buzz), held at full level for
20 ms and faded to silence over the next 60 ms; the first frame decoded
after the loss is cross-faded with the continued concealment.

An active frame whose range decode fails no longer commits its predictor,
CELP and postfilter state: the state is put back as it was before the
frame and the frame is concealed instead of played. A RED container that
cannot be unpacked is concealed too.

Tested: pitch found on synthetic tones, concealment follows the waveform,
fades to silence after 80 ms, keeps the duration asked at 16 and 48 kHz,
joins the next frame without a click; the 373 captured frames decode with
no frame taken for corrupt, and the reference correlation is unchanged.
